    "attribute": "arrangement",
    "likely_right_file": "bhel/Part1.pdf",
    "likely_right_page": 44,
    "why": "Both 1W+1S and 2X100% actually mean the same thing (two 100%-capacity pumps, one working and one standby), though Part 1 p.44 (backed by Part 4 p.61) states the operating philosophy more clearly.",
    "consequence": "Nothing goes wrong physically if 2X100% is treated as 1W+1S, as both provide 100% capacity per pump. However, if 2X100% is misread when adding a third pump (e.g., sizing pumps differently or running multiple pumps together), the discharge piping could be over-pressurized or the power supply overloaded."
   }
